Sean McAfee <eefacm@gmail.com> writes:

> Open question: What's the closest you've ever come to ascending, but
> didn't quite make it?
> Anyone get killed just a few steps from the right altar?  Or get killed
> while actually standing on the altar?

Yes, on the altar.
This was because of a stupid ascension trick: 
When a new version comes out and I make my first ascension on that
version, I want to bring an ice box filled with a sixpack of potions of
booze with my to the demigod bar.
I usually do it by sparing a wish and using it for the icebox at the
high altar of my god, so I don't need to carry the heavy icebox around.

Once (I don't remember any more whether it was when 3.4.3 was new or
with some earlier version) the ice box I received with the wish
contained some heavy corpses so it dropped and I wasn't able to lift it.
So I tried to pull the corpses out first, hoping to reduce the weight.
But there was a dragon corpse that I wasn't able to lift.
There was another wish left and I used it, but the next ice box was
loaded with heavy meat as well. I may have had even more wishes left, 
I don't remember that either.
Finally, after using my wishes, I got naked and dropped EVERYTHING from
my inventory and I still couldn't get the heavy corpse out.
Then came one of the riders, I don't remember which one. I whacked it a
few times with my bare hands, but it killed me.

Even when the rider was beating me, I still could have ascended if I
just had picked up the damn amulet and sacrificed it (and that would
have been another stupid ascension trick: ascending without anything
in my inventory), but instead I just used my bare hands against the
rider. 

I wasn't even annoyed by that stupid death, I felt only amused.

